{"id":"9bf47597f810702598ddc989337f282e29bfb817","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"9bf47597f810702598ddc989337f282e29bfb817","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"changelogs/current/new_features/dynamic_modules__bootstrap-runtime-update-string.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@","+Added string values to the runtime update notifications of the dynamic module bootstrap extension.","+A watched runtime key whose value is a non-empty string that is neither a number nor a boolean is now","+reported through the new ``envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update`` hook,","+instead of counting as unset, and the new ``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string``","+callback reads a runtime value as its text. The Rust SDK adds ``RuntimeValue::String`` and","+``get_runtime_string``. See","+:ref:`Runtime Updates <config_bootstrap_extensions_dynamic_modules_runtime_update>`."],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/configuration/other_features/bootstrap_extensions/dynamic_modules.rst","lines":["@@ -90,8 +90,12 @@ getters read it:","   read by ``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_number``."," * ``envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_bool_update`` for a boolean, as read by","   ``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_bool``.","+* ``envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update`` for a non-empty string that","+  reads as neither a number nor a boolean, as read by","+  ``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string``, which reads a value of any type as its text.","+  The text of a structured value that is not a fractional percent is unspecified."," ","-A value of any other type, such as a string, counts as unset. When a key becomes unset, Envoy calls","+A value of any other type, such as an empty string or null, counts as unset. When a key becomes unset, Envoy calls"," the hook of its previous type with the previous value and ``removed`` set. Envoy compares each"," newly loaded runtime snapshot with the previous values of the watched keys, so an RTDS update, a"," disk layer update or a request to the admin ``/runtime_modify`` endpoint reports only the watched","@@ -105,7 +109,7 @@ The extension can only watch keys during"," ``envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_server_initialized``. RTDS may or may not have"," delivered its layers by then, so the extension should read the current value with the runtime"," getters when it starts watching a key, and then rely on the hooks for the later changes. No update","-is reported once the server began to shut down. In the Rust SDK, the three hooks call","+is reported once the server began to shut down. In the Rust SDK, the four hooks call"," ``on_runtime_update`` of ``BootstrapExtension`` with a ``RuntimeValue``, or with ``None`` when the"," key became unset."," "],"additions":6,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/extension.cc","lines":["@@ -57,7 +57,8 @@ void DynamicModuleBootstrapExtension::onWorkerThreadInitialized() {"," bool DynamicModuleBootstrapExtension::enableRuntimeUpdate(absl::string_view key) {","   if (config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_bool_update_ == nullptr &&","       config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_int_update_ == nullptr &&","-      config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update_ == nullptr) {","+      config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update_ == nullptr &&","+      config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update_ == nullptr) {","     ENVOY_LOG(error, \"cannot enable runtime update since the module implements none of the \"","                      \"envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_*_update hooks\");","     return false;","@@ -108,6 +109,10 @@ DynamicModuleBootstrapExtension::runtimeValue(const Runtime::Snapshot& snapshot,","     if (value.bool_value_.has_value()) {","       return RuntimeValue(absl::in_place_type<bool>, *value.bool_value_);","     }","+    // A fractional percent is a structured value, which the string hook does not report.","+    if (!value.fractional_percent_value_.has_value() && !value.raw_string_value_.empty()) {","+      return RuntimeValue(absl::in_place_type<std::string>, value.raw_string_value_);","+    }","     return std::nullopt;","   }","   return std::nullopt;","@@ -136,9 +141,15 @@ void DynamicModuleBootstrapExtension::reportRuntimeUpdate(absl::string_view key,","       config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_int_update_(","           thisAsVoidPtr(), in_module_extension_, key_buffer, absl::get<uint64_t>(value), removed);","     }","-  } else if (config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update_ != nullptr) {","-    config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update_(","-        thisAsVoidPtr(), in_module_extension_, key_buffer, absl::get<double>(value), removed);","+  } else if (absl::holds_alternative<double>(value)) {","+    if (config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update_ != nullptr) {","+      config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update_(","+          thisAsVoidPtr(), in_module_extension_, key_buffer, absl::get<double>(value), removed);","+    }","+  } else if (config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update_ != nullptr) {","+    const std::string& text = absl::get<std::string>(value);","+    config_->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update_(","+        thisAsVoidPtr(), in_module_extension_, key_buffer, {text.data(), text.size()}, removed);","   }"," }"," "],"additions":15,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/extension.h","lines":["@@ -105,11 +105,11 @@ class DynamicModuleBootstrapExtension : public Server::BootstrapExtension,","   Server::ServerLifecycleNotifier::HandlePtr post_init_handle_;"," ","   // The value of a watched runtime key, typed the way the runtime update hooks report it: a","-  // boolean, a non-negative integer or any other number.","-  using RuntimeValue = absl::variant<bool, uint64_t, double>;","+  // boolean, a non-negative integer, any other number or a non-empty string.","+  using RuntimeValue = absl::variant<bool, uint64_t, double, std::string>;"," ","   // Returns the value of the key from the topmost layer of the snapshot that sets it, or nothing","-  // when that value is neither a boolean nor a number.","+  // when that value is none of those types.","   static std::optional<RuntimeValue> runtimeValue(const Runtime::Snapshot& snapshot,","                                                   absl::string_view key);"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/extension_config.cc","lines":["@@ -891,6 +891,11 @@ newDynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig(","           \"envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update\");","   config->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update_ =","       on_runtime_number_update.ok() ? on_runtime_number_update.value() : nullptr;","+  auto on_runtime_string_update =","+      config->dynamic_module_->getFunctionPointer<OnBootstrapExtensionRuntimeStringUpdateType>(","+          \"envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update\");","+  config->on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update_ =","+      on_runtime_string_update.ok() ? on_runtime_string_update.value() : nullptr;"," ","   // Always register an init target so that Envoy blocks traffic until the module signals readiness.","   // This must happen before calling the module constructor so the module can call"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/extension_config.h","lines":["@@ -90,6 +90,8 @@ using OnBootstrapExtensionRuntimeIntUpdateType =","     decltype(&envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_int_update);"," using OnBootstrapExtensionRuntimeNumberUpdateType =","     decltype(&envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update);","+using OnBootstrapExtensionRuntimeStringUpdateType =","+    decltype(&envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update);"," "," class DynamicModuleBootstrapExtension;"," ","@@ -369,6 +371,8 @@ class DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig","   OnBootstrapExtensionRuntimeIntUpdateType on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_int_update_ = nullptr;","   OnBootstrapExtensionRuntimeNumberUpdateType on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update_ =","       nullptr;","+  OnBootstrapExtensionRuntimeStringUpdateType on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update_ =","+      nullptr;"," ","   // The name of the extension.","   const std::string extension_name_;"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/abi/abi.h","lines":["@@ -867,6 +867,26 @@ uint64_t envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_int(envoy_dynamic_module_type"," double envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_number(envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer key,","                                                         double default_value);"," ","+/**","+ * envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string is called by the module to read a runtime value","+ * as a string, which is the text of the value in the topmost layer that sets the key. A number or a","+ * boolean has a text too, for example \"80\" or \"true\", so this reads a value of any type. Unlike the","+ * callbacks above it takes no default value: the result tells whether the key has a value.","+ *","+ * @param key is the runtime key to look up.","+ * @param result is the pointer to the buffer variable where the text of the value will be stored.","+ * It is left untouched when this returns false.","+ * @return true if the key has a value, false if the key does not exist or the runtime is not","+ * reachable from the calling thread.","+ *","+ * Note that the buffer stored in result is owned by Envoy, and it is guaranteed to be valid until","+ * the end of the current event hook. A module that needs the text for longer must copy it.","+ * As for the callbacks above, key must not name one of Envoy's own `envoy.reloadable_features.*`","+ * or `envoy.restart_features.*` guards.","+ */","+bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string(","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer key, envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer* result);","+"," // ----------------------------- Function Registry -----------------------------"," "," /**","@@ -10936,7 +10956,10 @@ void envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_get_active_resource_names"," //    envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update. An integer is not reported"," //    as a boolean, though envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_bool also reads it as one."," //  * A boolean is reported through envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_bool_update.","-//  * Any other value, such as a string, counts as unset.","+//  * A non-empty string that reads as neither a number nor a boolean is reported through","+//    envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update. The text of a structured","+//    value that is not a fractional percent is unspecified.","+//  * Any other value, such as an empty string or null, counts as unset."," //"," // Envoy loads a new runtime snapshot whenever a layer of the `layered_runtime` bootstrap option"," // changes, for example on an RTDS update, a disk layer update or a request to the admin","@@ -10993,6 +11016,17 @@ void envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_number_update(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_module_ptr extension_module_ptr,","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer key, double value, bool removed);"," ","+/**","+ * envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update is called when a watched","+ * runtime key gets a new string value, or becomes unset after having one. The value is owned by","+ * Envoy and valid only for the duration of the call.","+ */","+void envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update(","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_envoy_ptr extension_envoy_ptr,","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_module_ptr extension_module_ptr,","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer key, envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer value,","+    bool removed);","+"," /**","  * envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_enable_runtime_update is called by the module","  * to watch a runtime key, so that the runtime update hooks above are called on the bootstrap"],"additions":35,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/abi_impl.cc","lines":["@@ -166,6 +166,21 @@ double envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_number(envoy_dynamic_module_typ","   return snapshot->getDouble(absl::string_view(key.ptr, key.length), default_value);"," }"," ","+bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string(","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer key, envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer* result) {","+  const auto snapshot = currentRuntimeSnapshot();","+  if (!snapshot.has_value()) {","+    return false;","+  }","+  const auto value = snapshot->get(absl::string_view(key.ptr, key.length));","+  if (!value.has_value()) {","+    return false;","+  }","+  result->ptr = value->data();","+  result->length = value->size();","+  return true;","+}","+"," // ---------------------- Function registry callbacks --------------------------------"," "," bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_register_function(envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer key,"],"additions":15,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust/src/abi.rs","lines":["@@ -982,6 +982,28 @@ unsafe extern \"C\" {","     ) -> f64;"," }"," #[cfg_attr(envoy_dynamic_module_dll, link(name = \"envoy\", kind = \"raw-dylib\"))]","+unsafe extern \"C\" {","+    /** envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string is called by the module to read a runtime value","+ as a string, which is the text of the value in the topmost layer that sets the key. A number or a","+ boolean has a text too, for example \"80\" or \"true\", so this reads a value of any type. Unlike the","+ callbacks above it takes no default value: the result tells whether the key has a value.","+","+ @param key is the runtime key to look up.","+ @param result is the pointer to the buffer variable where the text of the value will be stored.","+ It is left untouched when this returns false.","+ @return true if the key has a value, false if the key does not exist or the runtime is not","+ reachable from the calling thread.","+","+ Note that the buffer stored in result is owned by Envoy, and it is guaranteed to be valid until","+ the end of the current event hook. A module that needs the text for longer must copy it.","+ As for the callbacks above, key must not name one of Envoy's own `envoy.reloadable_features.*`","+ or `envoy.restart_features.*` guards.*/","+    pub fn envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string(","+        key: envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer,","+        result: *mut envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer,","+    ) -> bool;","+}","+#[cfg_attr(envoy_dynamic_module_dll, link(name = \"envoy\", kind = \"raw-dylib\"))]"," unsafe extern \"C\" {","     /** envoy_dynamic_module_callback_register_function registers an opaque function pointer under the","  given key in the process-wide function registry. This allows modules loaded in the same process","@@ -11385,6 +11407,19 @@ unsafe extern \"C\" {","     );"," }"," #[cfg_attr(envoy_dynamic_module_dll, link(name = \"envoy\", kind = \"raw-dylib\"))]","+unsafe extern \"C\" {","+    /** envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update is called when a watched","+ runtime key gets a new string value, or becomes unset after having one. The value is owned by","+ Envoy and valid only for the duration of the call.*/","+    pub fn envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update(","+        extension_envoy_ptr: envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_envoy_ptr,","+        extension_module_ptr: envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_module_ptr,","+        key: envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer,","+        value: envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer,","+        removed: bool,","+    );","+}","+#[cfg_attr(envoy_dynamic_module_dll, link(name = \"envoy\", kind = \"raw-dylib\"))]"," unsafe extern \"C\" {","     /** envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_enable_runtime_update is called by the module","  to watch a runtime key, so that the runtime update hooks above are called on the bootstrap"],"additions":35,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust/src/bootstrap.rs","lines":["@@ -801,7 +801,7 @@ pub trait EnvoyBootstrapExtension {"," }"," "," /// The value of a watched runtime key, as given to [`BootstrapExtension::on_runtime_update`].","-#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]","+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]"," pub enum RuntimeValue {","   /// A boolean, as read by [`crate::get_runtime_bool`].","   Bool(bool),","@@ -810,6 +810,10 @@ pub enum RuntimeValue {","   Int(u64),","   /// Any other number, as read by [`crate::get_runtime_number`].","   Number(f64),","+  /// A non-empty string that reads as neither a number nor a boolean, as read by","+  /// [`crate::get_runtime_string`]. The text of a structured value that is not a fractional","+  /// percent is unspecified.","+  String(String),"," }"," "," /// BootstrapExtensionConfig is the module-side bootstrap extension configuration.","@@ -1200,10 +1204,10 @@ pub trait BootstrapExtension: Send + Sync {","   /// * `envoy_extension` can be used to interact with the underlying Envoy extension object.","   /// * `key` is the watched runtime key whose value changed.","   /// * `value` is the new value of the key, typed the way the runtime getters read it, or `None`","-  ///   when the key became unset. A value that is neither a boolean nor a number counts as unset.","-  ///   See [`RuntimeValue`]. When a runtime guard becomes unset, the guard returns to its value","-  ///   before any layer set it, normally its compiled default, while [`crate::get_runtime_bool`]","-  ///   returns the default given by the caller.","+  ///   when the key became unset. A value that is none of a boolean, a number or a non-empty string","+  ///   counts as unset. See [`RuntimeValue`]. When a runtime guard becomes unset, the guard returns","+  ///   to its value before any layer set it, normally its compiled default, while","+  ///   [`crate::get_runtime_bool`] returns the default given by the caller.","   fn on_runtime_update(","     &mut self,","     _envoy_extension: &mut dyn EnvoyBootstrapExtension,","@@ -2776,6 +2780,23 @@ ffi_export! {","   }"," }"," ","+ffi_export! {","+  /// Event hook called by Envoy when a watched runtime key gets a new string value, or becomes","+  /// unset after having one.","+  fn envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update(","+    envoy_ptr: abi::envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_envoy_ptr,","+    extension_ptr: abi::envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_module_ptr,","+    key: abi::envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer,","+    value: abi::envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer,","+    removed: bool,","+  ) {","+    let text =","+      unsafe { crate::ffi_helpers::str_lossy_from_raw(value.ptr as *const u8, value.length) };","+    let value = RuntimeValue::String(text.into_owned());","+    on_runtime_update_impl(envoy_ptr, extension_ptr, key, value, removed);","+  }","+}","+"," ffi_export! {","   /// Forwards an xDS outcome to the bootstrap config.","   ///"],"additions":26,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -264,6 +264,35 @@ pub fn get_runtime_number(key: &str, default_value: f64) -> f64 {","   }"," }"," ","+/// Read a runtime value as a string: the text of the value in the topmost layer that sets the key.","+/// A number or a boolean has a text too, for example `\"80\"` or `\"true\"`, so this reads a value of","+/// any type. See [`get_runtime_bool`] for the description of the runtime and the threading","+/// behavior, which are identical here.","+///","+/// Unlike the functions above, this takes no default value: it returns `None` when the key does not","+/// exist or the runtime is not reachable from the calling thread. A value that is not valid UTF-8","+/// is converted lossily.","+///","+/// Note that, as with [`get_runtime_int`], `key` must not name one of Envoy's own","+/// `envoy.reloadable_features.*` or `envoy.restart_features.*` guards; read those with","+/// [`get_runtime_bool`] instead.","+pub fn get_runtime_string(key: &str) -> Option<String> {","+  let mut result = abi::envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer {","+    ptr: std::ptr::null(),","+    length: 0,","+  };","+  let found = unsafe {","+    abi::envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string(str_to_module_buffer(key), &mut result)","+  };","+  if !found {","+    return None;","+  }","+  // The buffer is owned by Envoy and valid until the end of the current event hook, so copy it.","+  Some(","+    unsafe { ffi_helpers::str_lossy_from_raw(result.ptr as *const u8, result.length) }.into_owned(),","+  )","+}","+"," /// Register a function pointer under a name in the process-wide function registry."," ///"," /// This allows modules loaded in the same process to expose functions that other modules can"],"additions":29,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/sdk/rust/src/lib_test.rs","lines":["@@ -105,6 +105,51 @@ pub extern \"C\" fn envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_number(","     .unwrap_or(default_value)"," }"," ","+static MOCK_RUNTIME_STRINGS: std::sync::Mutex<Option<std::collections::HashMap<String, String>>> =","+  std::sync::Mutex::new(None);","+// Keeps the text last handed out alive, as Envoy's buffer is until the end of the hook. A later","+// call replaces it, so nothing is leaked.","+static MOCK_RUNTIME_STRING_RESULT: std::sync::Mutex<String> = std::sync::Mutex::new(String::new());","+","+#[no_mangle]","+pub extern \"C\" fn envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string(","+  key: abi::envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer,","+  result: *mut abi::envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer,","+) -> bool {","+  let guard = MOCK_RUNTIME_STRINGS.lock().unwrap();","+  let Some(value) = guard","+    .as_ref()","+    .and_then(|values| values.get(&module_buffer_to_string(key)))","+  else {","+    return false;","+  };","+  let mut stored = MOCK_RUNTIME_STRING_RESULT.lock().unwrap();","+  *stored = value.clone();","+  unsafe {","+    (*result).ptr = stored.as_ptr() as *const _;","+    (*result).length = stored.len();","+  }","+  true","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn test_runtime_string_callback() {","+  *MOCK_RUNTIME_STRINGS.lock().unwrap() = Some(std::collections::HashMap::from([","+    (","+      \"some.mapping\".to_string(),","+      \"80:15100,8080:15101\".to_string(),","+    ),","+    (\"some.empty\".to_string(), String::new()),","+  ]));","+  assert_eq!(","+    get_runtime_string(\"some.mapping\").as_deref(),","+    Some(\"80:15100,8080:15101\")","+  );","+  // A key that exists with an empty text is not a missing key.","+  assert_eq!(get_runtime_string(\"some.empty\").as_deref(), Some(\"\"));","+  assert_eq!(get_runtime_string(\"missing.key\"), None);","+}","+"," #[test]"," fn test_runtime_callbacks() {","   *MOCK_RUNTIME_BOOLS.lock().unwrap() = Some(std::collections::HashMap::from([","@@ -8973,12 +9018,31 @@ fn test_bootstrap_extension_runtime_update() {","     1.5,","     true,","   );","+  envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update(","+    std::ptr::null_mut(),","+    extension_ptr,","+    buffer(\"some.mapping\"),","+    buffer(\"80:15100,8080:15101\"),","+    false,","+  );","+  envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_runtime_string_update(","+    std::ptr::null_mut(),","+    extension_ptr,","+    buffer(\"some.text\"),","+    buffer(\"previous text\"),","+    true,","+  );","   assert_eq!(","     *UPDATES.lock().unwrap(),","     vec![","       (\"some.flag\".to_string(), Some(RuntimeValue::Bool(true))),","       (\"some.int\".to_string(), Some(RuntimeValue::Int(42))),","       (\"some.number\".to_string(), None),","+      (","+        \"some.mapping\".to_string(),","+        Some(RuntimeValue::String(\"80:15100,8080:15101\".to_string()))","+      ),","+      (\"some.text\".to_string(), None),","     ]","   );"," "],"additions":64,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/extensions/dynamic_modules/abi_impl_test.cc","lines":["@@ -574,6 +574,44 @@ TEST(CommonAbiImplTest, GetRuntimeMissingKeyReturnsDefault) {","   EXPECT_DOUBLE_EQ(2.5, envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_number(key, 2.5));"," }"," ","+TEST(CommonAbiImplTest, GetRuntimeStringReturnsTheTextOfTheValue) {","+  testing::NiceMock<Server::Configuration::MockServerFactoryContext> context;","+  const std::string text = \"80:15100,8080:15101\";","+  EXPECT_CALL(context.runtime_loader_.snapshot_, get(absl::string_view(\"some.mapping\")))","+      .WillOnce(Return(Envoy::Runtime::Snapshot::ConstStringOptRef(text)));","+","+  ScopedThreadLocalServerContextSetter setter(context);","+  envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer key = {\"some.mapping\", 12};","+  envoy_dynamic_module_type_envoy_buffer result = {nullptr, 0};","+  ASSERT_TRUE(envoy_dynamic_module_callback_get_runtime_string(key, &result));","+  EXPECT_EQ(text, absl::string_view(result.ptr, result.length));","+}","+","+TEST(CommonAbiImplTest, GetRuntimeStringOfMissingKeyLeavesTheResult) {","+  testing::NiceMock<Server::Configuration::MockServerFactoryContext> context;","+  ON_CALL(context.runtime_loader_.snapshot_, get(testing::_))","+      .WillByDefault(Return(Envoy::Runtime::Snapshot::ConstStringOptRef()));","+","+  ScopedThreadLocalServerContextSetter setter(context);","+  envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buff